<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 2.x Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="_Toc235450352" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 1 — Bold used for general emphasis</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider an HTML paragraph that reads: "The Server Management module is used to manage various</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>general</keyword>
        <keyword>emphasis</keyword>
        <keyword>Server</keyword>
        <keyword>Management</keyword>
        <keyword>Bold</keyword>
        <keyword>module</keyword>
        <indexterm>general</indexterm>
        <indexterm>emphasis</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Server</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>
      <section>
      <p>Consider an HTML paragraph that reads: "The Server Management module is used to manage various virtual servers." The term "Server Management" is wrapped in a <codeph>&lt;strong&gt;</codeph> element for general emphasis.</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Bold used for general emphasis</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>HTML Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;p>
  The &lt;strong>Server Management&lt;/strong> module is used to manage various virtual servers.
&lt;/p></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;p>
    The &lt;b>Server Management&lt;/b> module is used to manage various virtual servers.
&lt;/p></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
<p><b>Result:</b> The converter maps <codeph>&lt;strong&gt;</codeph> used for general emphasis to <codeph>&lt;b&gt;</codeph> within the surrounding <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> element.</p>
         </section>
   </refbody>
</reference>
